              "output": "<path>/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_HW2/.opencode/command/debugging.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: description: Analyse a Python error or buggy function and propose a fix.\n3: agent: Python_expert\n4: ---\n5: \n6: ## Task: Debug Python code\n7: \n8: The user gives you broken code and a traceback, or points to a buggy file.\n9: \n10: 1. Explain the **root cause** in one beginner-friendly sentence (e.g. \u00ab\u0442\u044b \u043f\u043e\u043f\u0440\u043e\u0441\u0438\u043b 5-\u0439 \u044d\u043b\u0435\u043c\u0435\u043d\u0442 \u0441\u043f\u0438\u0441\u043a\u0430, \u0432 \u043a\u043e\u0442\u043e\u0440\u043e\u043c \u0432\u0441\u0435\u0433\u043e 3\u00bb).\n11: 2. Point to the exact line or expression that is wrong.\n12: 3. Provide the corrected code and 1\u20132 `assert` examples that now pass.\n13: 4. Add a **prevention note** \u2014 what to check next time so this bug does not repeat.\n14: 5. If the traceback hints at a missing import, assume standard library only.\n15: 6. When asked, save the fix proposal to `reports/<name>_debug.md`.\n\n(End of file - total 15 lines)\n</content>",
