            "raw_output": {
              "output": "<path>/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_HW2/.opencode/command/doc-writing.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: description: Add docstrings and documentation to existing Python code.\n3: agent: Python_expert\n4: ---\n5: \n6: ## Task: Document Python code\n7: \n8: The user gives you a file path or pastes a code snippet.\n9: \n10: 1. Read the code carefully \u2014 document only what is actually there. Do not guess or embellish.\n11: 2. Add a Google-style docstring to every function that does not already have one.\n12: 3. Each docstring includes:\n13:    - One sentence explaining *why* the function exists (its purpose).\n14:    - `Args:` \u2014 each parameter with its type and meaning.\n15:    - `Returns:` \u2014 the return type and what it means.\n16:    - `Raises:` \u2014 any exceptions the function may raise (if obvious from the code).\n17: 4. Do not change any logic \u2014 only add or improve comments and docstrings.\n18: 5. Use beginner-friendly language throughout.\n\n(End of file - total 18 lines)\n</content>",
              "metadata": {
                "truncated": false,
                "loaded": [],
                "preview": "---\ndescription: Add docstrings and documentation to existing Python code.\nagent: Python_expert\n---\n\n## Task: Document Python code\n\nThe user gives you a file path or pastes a code snippet.\n\n1. Read the code carefully \u2014 document only what is actually there. Do not guess or embellish.\n2. Add a Google-style docstring to every function that does not already have one.\n3. Each docstring includes:\n   - One sentence explaining *why* the function exists (its purpose).\n   - `Args:` \u2014 each parameter with its type and meaning.\n   - `Returns:` \u2014 the return type and what it means.\n   - `Raises:` \u2014 any exceptions the function may raise (if obvious from the code).\n4. Do not change any logic \u2014 only add or improve comments and docstrings.\n5. Use beginner-friendly language throughout.",
                "display": {
                  "lineStart": 1.0,
                  "type": "file",
                  "text": "---\ndescription: Add docstrings and documentation to existing Python code.\nagent: Python_expert\n---\n\n## Task: Document Python code\n\nThe user gives you a file path or pastes a code snippet.\n\n1. Read the code carefully \u2014 document only what is actually there. Do not guess or embellish.\n2. Add a Google-style docstring to every function that does not already have one.\n3. Each docstring includes:\n   - One sentence explaining *why* the function exists (its purpose).\n   - `Args:` \u2014 each parameter with its type and meaning.\n   - `Returns:` \u2014 the return type and what it means.\n   - `Raises:` \u2014 any exceptions the function may raise (if obvious from the code).\n4. Do not change any logic \u2014 only add or improve comments and docstrings.\n5. Use beginner-friendly language throughout.",
