              "output": "<path>/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_HW2/.opencode/command/function-writing.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: description: Write a new Python function from a short specification.\n3: agent: Python_expert\n4: ---\n5: \n6: ## Task: Write a Python function\n7: \n8: The user gives you a specification \u2014 inputs, output, and expected behaviour.\n9: \n10: 1. Read the target file first if one is named; otherwise write a standalone function.\n11: 2. Write clean, runnable Python with:\n12:    - Type hints on every parameter and the return value.\n13:    - A one-line docstring describing what the function does.\n14:    - 2\u20133 `assert` statements at the bottom that prove correctness.\n15: 3. Handle edge cases explicitly: empty list, 0, None, negative numbers.\n16: 4. Never use libraries that are not already imported in the project.\n17: 5. If the user names a file, append the function there; otherwise propose a new file.\n\n(End of file - total 17 lines)\n</content>",
              "metadata": {
                "loaded": [],
                "display": {
                  "lineStart": 1.0,
